# GUARD DASHBOARD

# Application URL: http://localhost:3000
# Guard Login URL: http://localhost:3000/login
# Guard Dashboard URL: http://localhost:3000/security/dashboard (navigating to http://localhost:3000/security automatically redirects to /security/dashboard)
# Guard Signup URL: http://localhost:3000/signup (Guards begin by creating an account here)
# Guard Account Creation/Approval Process:
# Self-Registration Constraint: In 

# lib/server/auth.ts
# , the public signup endpoint (/signup) strictly restricts self-assigned roles to visitor or student.
# Application Submission: The applicant creates an account at /signup, then submits a guard registration profile via the guard registration flow (POST /api/guards/registrations).
# Admin Review & Approval: The Administrator logs into http://localhost:3000/admin/guards and opens the Registrations tab.
# Activation: Upon clicking Approve, the system:
# Assigns a guard identifier (GRD-xxx) in security_guards.
# Updates the applicant's role in public.profiles to security.
# Sets active = true.
# (Direct Creation): An admin can also add a guard directly via the Add Guard dialog on 

# /admin/guards
# .
# Password Reset Instructions:
# Open http://localhost:3000/forgot-password.
# Enter the registered guard's email address.
# Check the inbox for the reset link and complete the password reset at /reset-password.
# Alternatively, the Administrator can assist via the Supabase Auth user management console.
# VERIFICATION

# Local or deployed: Local. Configured via NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000. Git remote points to https://github.com/Nikhil6306/campus-security-Mng-system.git. No live production domain is configured in the environment files.
# Authentication provider: Supabase Auth (@supabase/supabase-js) connected to https://qpamgfhggxwctoibmsbl.supabase.co with role synchronization in public.profiles. An automated fallback to local SQLite (.data/campus-security.db) exists for offline or testing mode.
# Admin route protection: Verified. Protected by 

# AdminShell
# . Any non-admin role attempting to access /admin/* is blocked and redirected to their respective portal (/security/dashboard, /teacher/dashboard, etc.). All administrative server endpoints verify ADMIN_ROLES (admin, super_admin) server-side.
# Guard route protection: Verified. Protected by 

# SecurityShell
# . Only accounts with role security (or admin) are permitted. Unauthenticated users are redirected to /login?next=..., and unauthorized users are redirected away. Server API routes enforce GATE_ROLES.
# Issues found:
# The local server is currently not running (port 3000 is inactive).
# The demo accounts in 

# lib/demo-accounts.ts
#  (admin@dsvv.edu.in, security@dsvv.edu.in) are mock UI helpers; real access in Supabase mode requires the registered credentials in Supabase Auth.
# Exact steps to log in:
